- op: discuss  # bbf1
  at: '2026-09-22T04:34:57Z'  # bbf1
  by: agent  # bbf1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bbf1
  clock: 4  # bbf1
  nonce: bbf1  # bbf1
  message: "DONE, merged to dev. py.py gained the FIFTH is_exported site: a method's verdict is (class_is_exported AND not private-by-name), reusing _python_visibility_modifiers -- the same call that fills this symbol's modifiers -- so the two facts cannot disagree.\n\nRESULT: 24,929 python methods, 0 null (24,048 True / 881 False). Verified END TO END through 'hypergumbo survey', not just at the analyzer: the value survives finalize.py, which only ever narrows a non-public symbol to False and never contradicts it.\n\nTHE OPEN QUESTION FROM MY EARLIER NOTE IS ANSWERED. I said I had not chased which pass wrote the 668 False. It is finalize.py:737 -- compute_visibility returns non-public for a leading-underscore name, and the next line sets is_exported=False. The same pass then STRIPS visibility terms from modifiers, which is why those records showed empty modifiers in the map and made the mechanism hard to see.\n\nDISCLOSED CONSEQUENCE, measured as a clean A/B on identical trees (production functions identical at 5,964, so the only variable is this change):\n  seeds     1,541 -> 2,303   (+762)\n  dead      2,468 ->   448   (-2,020)\n  dead%      41.4% ->  7.5%\n  __init__     34 ->     0\n  demoted      96 ->    25\n2,026 candidates disappear: 785 methods directly, 1,241 functions they transitively reach. This REMOVES the 34 __init__ candidates INV-hugit had just made visible.\n\nI did not take this decision alone -- it collided with the standing rule that loosening a withholding gate is the false-all-clear direction. Owner was shown these numbers and ruled SHIP AS-IS, DISCLOSE LOUDLY. The defence is that 41.4% rested on an ABSENT measurement rather than a negative one, and the rule is the same one already applied to top-level functions and classes.\n\nRESIDUAL WORTH KNOWING: a public Python method is now essentially unreportable as dead under --seeds production. If that proves too quiet, the lever is the seed policy, not this field.\n\nRecorded scip-python fixture pin moved is_exported 6 -> 10 of 10; its comment had been recording this producer gap as a property of the comparison.\nSuite: 4,135 passed, 1 pin updated, changed sources 100%, ratchet clean."  # bbf1
